Package: dnsinfo
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: dhtech <dhtech@users.noreply.github.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: adduser, bind9
Section: net
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/dhtech/dnsinfo
Description: counts which domains a name server is asked for
 dnsinfo listens on a unix socket for the dnstap stream of a name
 server (BIND 9), cuts every name asked for down to its domain and
 keeps a counter per domain and hour in a PostgreSQL database. Nothing
 about who asked is kept.
 .
 One static binary and the unit dnsinfo.service, which runs it as a
 user of its own, "dnsinfo". It depends on bind9 for the group "bind",
 which the socket is given to. A first
 installation neither enables nor starts it: it needs a database first
 (DNSINFO_DSN in /etc/default/dnsinfo).
